PRETABLE11 ADDENDUM 2 -- written 2026-09-06 ~12:0x, BEFORE table 11 runs (table 4 of lunaabsentcpu still holds the CPU), as a SEPARATE
file so PRETABLE11's own mtime stays the proof of order.  Source: grok's pass-7 answer (ONE MORE REPAIR), read in full.

THE CLASS.  The SFRZ re-route predicate READS PSR (`if (cpu->cd.m88k.cr[M88K_CR_PSR] & M88K_PSR_SFRZ)`), so a PSR-bit conjunct THERE is a
narrowing on a body-read lvalue -- clause (d) floor -- unlike the switch-1 `implemented' arms, which read no PSR bit (v12 disclosed those
as clause (e) with M_MISNOC measured).  Every SFRZ-set row reached the re-route with IND SET and C CLEAR: the first delivery leaves PSR =
0x8000000b, and the handler-stcr rows write 0x80000003 / 0x00000003.  So `(PSR & SFRZ) && (PSR & IND)' and `(PSR & SFRZ) && !(PSR & C)'
are predicted 41/41 on v10 and 44/44 on v12: a total escape of the shipped composite.  MODE and SFD1 already vary at the re-route (errpriv
MODE clear; errdiv0 SFD1 clear), so the open cells are exactly IND and C.  MXM / BO cannot be set by stcr without stopping the cpu; the
88110-only bits are 88100 here -- disclosed.

ROWS (dual to resid50ind / resid50c at the fallback):
  errind  first fault div0; handler = stcr r4,cr1 (r4 = 0x80000009: MODE|SFD1|SFRZ, IND CLEAR) then `ld r6,r5,0' with r5 = DATA+1 (odd).
          Fix: MISALIGNED with SFRZ set -> re-route -> ERROR at 0x50, shadows frozen (sxip 0x10004|V), refatal line PRESENT.
          Under M_RRIND: IND clear -> no re-route -> MISALIGNED delivered to 0x20 with the shadows frozen and NO refatal line ->
          the row reds on RESULT (breakpoint at 0x50 never reached; STOP) -- the channel is the entry pc, with refatal as the second channel.
  errc    same shape, r4 = 0x9000000b (C|MODE|SFD1|IND|SFRZ).  Under M_RRNOC: C set -> no re-route -> delivered to 0x20 -> STOP.
  Both rows use STCR_R4_CR1 = 0x80048024 (encoding checked against STCR_R5_CR1 = 0x80058025: S1 field 4 at bits 16..20 and 0..4).

MUTANTS (exact edits, on the re-route's inner condition `\t\tif (!is_trap) {'):
  M_RRIND   `if (!is_trap && (cpu->cd.m88k.cr[M88K_CR_PSR] & M88K_PSR_IND)) {'   predicted: v10 41/41, v12 44/44, v13 45/46 (errind STOP)
  M_RRNOC   `if (!is_trap && !(cpu->cd.m88k.cr[M88K_CR_PSR] & M88K_PSR_C)) {'    predicted: v10 41/41, v12 44/44, v13 45/46 (errc STOP)
  (grok also named the OUTER form `if ((PSR & SFRZ) && (PSR & IND))'; inner and outer differ only in whether update_shadow_regs is cleared
  for the IND-clear case -- under the outer form the shadows would be UNFROZEN too, an additional red on sxip -- so the INNER form is the
  quieter mutant and is the one built, per the least-observable-form rule.)

CHANNEL check (the fourth pre-table check): for each new row the observable that differs under its mutant is the ENTRY PC (0x50 vs 0x20),
observed as the breakpoint at 0x50 not being reached, plus the refatal line; both vary.  Not vacuous by construction.

Table 11 now runs SEVEN mutants (M_SFRZTRAP450 M_SFRZTRAP496 M_SFRZTRAPHI M_ERRORFRZON M_MISNOC M_RRIND M_RRNOC), WANT=46/46, frozen v13
md5 4192b7da; each also scored on the frozen v10 instrument so the sweeps are measurements.  The driver's expected-HALT dict is unchanged
(errind/errc are DELIVER rows).  Gate pins pre-set to 46/46, err(...|ind|c) count 6, trapfrozen(...|511)? count 11 -- the HEAD figure in the
gate's witness comment is updated only after the HEAD run in the table.
